From 42d93e03c21257b8f47b4b310ed4ec98d6a65492 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: dai <dai623815825@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 11 Aug 2026 22:39:04 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 1/6] arm64: add Rockchip RK3576 chip + GICv2 AMP-slave support

- New chip layer arch/arm64/src/rk3576 (+ include/rk3576): Cortex-A53
  AMP slave running at 0x41800000 alongside Linux on KickPi K7; MMU maps
  only the private carve-out, the Normal-NC shared-memory window and the
  peripheral window; no PSCI usage.
- CONFIG_ARM64_GIC_SLAVE (GICv2): skip the distributor global init
  entirely when a master OS owns the GIC-400 distributor; only banked
  CPU-interface setup and per-IRQ write-1-to-set operations remain.
